<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parnon</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Parnonas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parnon is a mountain range in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, running from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadia">Arcadia</a> south-east through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laconia">Laconia</a> and rising to about 1,935 metres. It closes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurotas">Eurotas</a> valley to the east, opposite the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taygetus">Taygetus</a> range, and separated ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> from the borderlands of Thyreatis and Kynouria disputed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parnon.jpg" alt="Parnon" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Housen · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20090729_parnonas06.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Sparta lay in the valley of the Eurotas River in Laconia, in the south-eastern Peloponnese, between the Taygetus and <b>Parnon</b> mountain ranges.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sparta">Sparta · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
